Description: SCos-styled lightweight X11 window manager
 scoswm is a small, non-compositing X11 window manager that manages
 ordinary Linux applications while looking and behaving like the SCos
 desktop: bottom taskbar with launcher, window picker, pins, power
 button and clock; real freedesktop icons on the desktop and taskbar;
 and the built-in Terminal/Files/SysMon/Settings core apps.
 .
 It installs /usr/share/xsessions/scoswm.desktop, so display managers
 such as SDDM offer "SCosWM" as a selectable X11 session at login.
 Clients keep full GPU acceleration through Xorg/GLX (NVIDIA
 proprietary and nouveau alike); there is no compositor.
